# More info: https://docs.docker.com/engine/reference/builder/#dockerignore-file
# Ignore everything by default and re-include only needed files
**

# Re-include Go source files (but not *_test.go)
!**/*.go
**/*_test.go

# Re-include Go module files
!go.mod
!go.sum

# Re-include files the Go build embeds. Without these the build fails at
# compile time with "pattern <file>: no matching files found", because an
# ignored file is absent from the context rather than merely unused - so no
# binary image could be built at all.
#
# internal/observation/schema.go embeds the normative observation schema: a
# sensor pod has no repository to read it from, and a schema loaded from a
# ConfigMap could drift from the code producing the records.
!internal/observation/observation.schema.json
